# MAIW wrapper sync — auto commit + push

When you change files in the **MAIW wrapper repo** (`d:\code\maiw` root — e.g. `memory/`,
`core/`, `.cursor/rules/`, `.claude/`, adapters, Confluence/Jira convention docs), keep
remote up to date **without waiting for the user to ask**.

This **includes** memory updates required after `apps/<name>/` code changes (see
`maiw-memory-after-code`). App commits in nested repos do **not** update wrapper memory —
you must write `memory/` here and push the wrapper, or the next machine/agent is blind.

## Policy (Cursor + Claude Code + Codex)

1. **Auto-commit and auto-push** wrapper changes in the same session. Do not leave durable
   memory/docs only local. Do not ask “should I push the wrapper?” — just do it.
2. Before/after commit: ensure Attribution is off and `git log -1 --format=full` has **no**
   AI `Co-authored-by` / `Made-with` trailer (`core/ATTRIBUTION.md`). Never change
   `git config` identity; never add AI as author.
3. If push is blocked (network, auth, secrets in the diff, or mixed with unrelated dirty
   files), tell the user once with the blocker — otherwise proceed.
4. Do **not** auto-commit or auto-push nested app repos under `apps/`. When app work left
   uncommitted or unpushed changes, **ask once** at the end of the turn, e.g. “Want me to
   commit and push `apps/<name>`?” — only proceed after they say yes.
